#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bench-kc-build -- link a boot kernel collection on Linux, in place of kmutil.

    bench-kc-build --kernel <path> [--kdk <path>] --kc-type <mac13g|...>
                   [--kernel-config DEVELOPMENT] [--arch arm64e]
                   [--kmbuildversion <str> | --ref-kc <path>]
                   [--text-exec-order kexts-first|kernel-first]
                   --out <path>

It drives dyld_app_cache_util, Apple's open-source collection builder from
dyld-1378 (base/darwin/toolchain/build-dyld-app-cache-util.sh), and composes the
__PRELINK_INFO extras kmutil adds, so the output is byte-identical to kmutil's
for the same inputs.  dyld_app_cache_util is looked up as $KCB_TOOL, then on
$PATH (/usr/bin, where macOS keeps kmutil).

  --kernel            the Mach-O kernel to build the collection around.  For
                      a kdk-* collection that is the KDK's own
                      System/Library/Kernels/kernel.<cfg>.<soc>.
  --kdk               the KDK root.  It MUST be at its real macOS path,
                      /Library/Developer/KDKs/KDK_<version>_<build>.kdk: the
                      path is embedded verbatim in every _PrelinkBundlePath
                      in __PRELINK_INFO, so mounting it anywhere else still
                      produces a correct collection but not a byte-identical
                      one.  (Bind-mount it; never copy it into a layer.)
                      Default: $KDKROOT, else the one
                      /Library/Developer/KDKs/KDK_$MACOS_VERSION_*.kdk
                      (MACOS_VERSION defaults to 26.5, as in linux-xnu-build).
  --kc-type           picks the KDK manifest whose requiredIdentifiers give
                      the kext include list: mac13g -> Apple silicon Mac.
  --kernel-config     DEVELOPMENT (default) | KASAN | RELEASE.  Lowercased, it is the
                      kext variant (`-kext-variant development`).
  $KC_FILTER          (environment) extended regex of bundle ids to drop
                      from the include list (grep -vE, as darwin-xnu-build's
                      KC_FILTER); a kernel compiled from the open-source tree
                      needs KC_FILTER=com.apple.driver.SEPHibernation.
  --kmbuildversion    the KMBuildVersion string kmutil stamps into
  / --ref-kc          __PRELINK_INFO, or a reference collection to read it
                      back out of.  It is host state, not a build input:
                      there is no kmutil on Linux to read it from.  With neither, the key is left out: xnu and
                      dyld never read it, but the KC is then not kmutil's
                      bytes.
  --text-exec-order   where the kexts' __TEXT_EXEC go inside the collection's:
                      kexts-first (default; dyld-1378 / 26.5 kmutil order, what
                      xnu >= 12377.121 accepts) or kernel-first (the older
                      order, the only one xnu <= 12377.81 / macOS 26.3 boots).
                      Also settable as $KCB_TEXT_EXEC_ORDER.
  --out               where to write the collection.
  --task / --variant / --soc
                      labels only; they name the collection in the log.

Three things kmutil does that dyld_app_cache_util does not, all done here:

1. Stage the KDK's Extensions with kmutil's Info.plists (stage()).

   `dyld_app_cache_util` copies each kext's Info.plist verbatim into the KC's
   __PRELINK_INFO `_PrelinkInfoDictionary`.  kmutil/KernelManagement does not: it
   first rewrites the dictionary.  Reproducing those rewrites is the whole
   difference between the two builders' __PRELINK_INFO, and the
   cheapest place to do it is *before* the tool runs -- mirror the Extensions
   tree with augmented Info.plists and point the builder at the mirror.

   The mirror is directories + symlinks, so it costs a few MB, not a KDK copy.  It is
   rooted so that `-volume-root <stage>` makes the builder's `_PrelinkBundlePath`
   come out as the real KDK path:

       <stage>/Library/Developer/KDKs/KDK_x.kdk/System/Library/Extensions/...
       -volume-root <stage>   ->   _PrelinkBundlePath = /Library/Developer/KDKs/...

   What kmutil adds to each kext's Info.plist:

     * arch overrides are folded down: any `<key>_arm64` and then `<key>_arm64e`
       replaces `<key>` (the suffixed keys stay).  This is what makes AppleSMC's
       OSBundleLibraries the ARM graph rather than the Intel one, and it also
       moves OSBundleCompatibleVersion_arm64 and IOKitPersonalities_arm64.
     * `_InfoPlistDigest` = raw SHA-256 of the Info.plist file's bytes, before
       any of this rewriting.
     * `OSBundleUUID` = the LC_UUID of the arm64e slice of the kext executable
       (the `_development` variant when one exists and -variant says so).
     * every personality in every `IOKitPersonalities*` dictionary gains
       `IOPersonalityPublisher` = the bundle id, and `CFBundleIdentifier` = the
       bundle id if it did not already have one.
     * a kext with no executable additionally gains `_CodelessKextBundlePath`
       (the bundle's absolute path), `OSBundleTeamIdentifier` (`None` when
       unsigned) and `kOSBundleDextUniqueIdentifier` = SHA-256 of that same
       absolute path string.

2. Filter the include list (filter_ids()).

   dyld_app_cache_util hard-errors on (a) an explicitly requested bundle id whose
   executable has no arm64e slice, and (b) the com.apple.kpi.* pseudo-kexts, whose
   KDK "executables" are plain-arm64e KPI stubs -- the builder resolves those from
   the kernel's __LINKINFO,__symbolsets instead.  kmutil/KernelManagement silently
   drops both.  Print the surviving ids, and the dropped ones to stderr.

3. Stamp KMBuildVersion, ManagerVersion and OSPrelinkInfoContainsUUIDs on the
   plist (-prelink-info-extra), and list every com.apple.kpi.* symbol set as a
   codeless bundle: their code comes from the kernel's __LINKINFO,__symbolsets,
   but kmutil still writes an Info.plist entry for each.

EULA: the output embeds Apple's kexts verbatim.  It is LOCAL ONLY and must
never be pushed to a registry.
"""

import argparse
import glob
import hashlib
import os
import plistlib
import re
import shutil
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile

CPU_TYPE_ARM64 = 0x0100000C
LC_UUID = 0x1B
FAT_MAGICS = (b'\xca\xfe\xba\xbe', b'\xca\xfe\xba\xbf')
MH_MAGIC_64_LE = b'\xcf\xfa\xed\xfe'

ARCH_SUFFIXES = {
    # applied in order, so the more specific spelling wins
    'arm64e': ('_arm64', '_arm64e'),
    'arm64': ('_arm64',),
    'x86_64': ('_x86_64',),
}


def _slices(f):
    """Yield (cputype, cpusubtype, offset) for each 64-bit little-endian slice."""
    f.seek(0)
    magic = f.read(4)
    if magic in FAT_MAGICS:
        wide = magic == b'\xca\xfe\xba\xbf'
        n = struct.unpack('>I', f.read(4))[0]
        entry = 32 if wide else 20
        raw = f.read(n * entry)
        for i in range(n):
            e = raw[i * entry:(i + 1) * entry]
            if wide:
                ct, cs, off = struct.unpack('>iiQ', e[:16])
            else:
                ct, cs, off = struct.unpack('>iiI', e[:12])
            yield ct & 0xFFFFFFFF, cs & 0xFFFFFFFF, off
    elif magic == MH_MAGIC_64_LE:
        ct, cs = struct.unpack('<II', f.read(8))
        yield ct, cs, 0


def macho_uuid(path, cputype=CPU_TYPE_ARM64, cpusubtype=2):
    """LC_UUID of the slice matching cputype/cpusubtype, or None."""
    try:
        with open(path, 'rb') as f:
            for ct, cs, off in list(_slices(f)):
                if ct != cputype or (cs & 0xFF) != cpusubtype:
                    continue
                f.seek(off + 16)
                ncmds, sizeofcmds = struct.unpack('<II', f.read(8))
                f.seek(off + 32)
                cmds = f.read(sizeofcmds)
                p = 0
                for _ in range(ncmds):
                    if p + 8 > len(cmds):
                        break
                    cmd, cmdsize = struct.unpack('<II', cmds[p:p + 8])
                    if cmd == LC_UUID:
                        return cmds[p + 8:p + 24]
                    if cmdsize == 0:
                        break
                    p += cmdsize
    except (OSError, struct.error):
        return None
    return None


def bundle_layout(kext):
    """(info_plist_path, executable_dir) for a .kext, honouring the flat layout."""
    for info_dir, exe_dir in ((os.path.join(kext, 'Contents'), os.path.join(kext, 'Contents', 'MacOS')),
                              (kext, kext)):
        info = os.path.join(info_dir, 'Info.plist')
        if os.path.isfile(info):
            return info, exe_dir
    return None, None


def augment(kext_path, info_path, exe_dir, arch, variant, real_bundle_path):
    """kmutil's version of a kext's Info.plist dictionary."""
    with open(info_path, 'rb') as f:
        raw = f.read()
    try:
        pl = plistlib.loads(raw)
    except Exception:
        return None
    if not isinstance(pl, dict):
        return None
    bundle_id = pl.get('CFBundleIdentifier')
    if not isinstance(bundle_id, str):
        return None

    out = dict(pl)

    # 1. fold the arch-specific overrides down onto the generic keys
    for suffix in ARCH_SUFFIXES.get(arch, ()):
        for key in list(pl.keys()):
            if key.endswith(suffix) and len(key) > len(suffix):
                out[key[:-len(suffix)]] = pl[key]

    # 2. IOPersonalityPublisher / CFBundleIdentifier on every personality
    for key, value in list(out.items()):
        if key != 'IOKitPersonalities' and not key.startswith('IOKitPersonalities_'):
            continue
        if not isinstance(value, dict):
            continue
        merged = {}
        for name, personality in value.items():
            if isinstance(personality, dict):
                personality = dict(personality)
                personality.setdefault('CFBundleIdentifier', bundle_id)
                personality['IOPersonalityPublisher'] = bundle_id
            merged[name] = personality
        out[key] = merged

    # 3. digest of the *original* bytes
    out['_InfoPlistDigest'] = hashlib.sha256(raw).digest()

    # 4. OSBundleUUID, or the codeless keys
    exe_name = out.get('CFBundleExecutable')
    exe_path = None
    if isinstance(exe_name, str) and exe_dir is not None:
        candidate = os.path.join(exe_dir, exe_name)
        if variant and os.path.isfile(candidate + '_' + variant):
            exe_path = candidate + '_' + variant
        elif os.path.isfile(candidate):
            exe_path = candidate
    if exe_path is not None:
        uuid = macho_uuid(exe_path)
        if uuid is not None:
            out['OSBundleUUID'] = uuid
    else:
        out['_CodelessKextBundlePath'] = real_bundle_path
        out.setdefault('OSBundleTeamIdentifier', 'None')
        out['kOSBundleDextUniqueIdentifier'] = hashlib.sha256(real_bundle_path.encode()).digest()

    return out


def stage(src_root, dst_root, real_root, arch, variant):
    """Mirror src_root into dst_root; real_root is src_root's path as kmutil sees it."""
    n_plists = 0
    n_links = 0
    for dirpath, dirnames, filenames in os.walk(src_root, followlinks=False):
        rel = os.path.relpath(dirpath, src_root)
        dst_dir = dst_root if rel == '.' else os.path.join(dst_root, rel)
        os.makedirs(dst_dir, exist_ok=True)
        # A symlinked directory is mirrored as a symlink; nothing inside a kext
        # in a KDK is one, but do not silently descend if that ever changes.
        for name in list(dirnames):
            full = os.path.join(dirpath, name)
            if os.path.islink(full):
                dirnames.remove(name)
                link = os.path.join(dst_dir, name)
                if not os.path.lexists(link):
                    os.symlink(full, link)
                    n_links += 1
        for name in filenames:
            src = os.path.join(dirpath, name)
            dst = os.path.join(dst_dir, name)
            if os.path.lexists(dst):
                continue
            handled = False
            if name == 'Info.plist':
                # only rewrite the Info.plist that *is* a bundle's Info.plist
                kext = os.path.dirname(dirpath) if os.path.basename(dirpath) == 'Contents' else dirpath
                if kext.endswith('.kext'):
                    info_path, exe_dir = bundle_layout(kext)
                    if info_path == src:
                        real_bundle = os.path.join(real_root, os.path.relpath(kext, src_root))
                        data = augment(kext, info_path, exe_dir, arch, variant, real_bundle)
                        if data is not None:
                            with open(dst, 'wb') as f:
                                plistlib.dump(data, f, fmt=plistlib.FMT_XML, sort_keys=True)
                            n_plists += 1
                            handled = True
            if not handled:
                os.symlink(src, dst)
                n_links += 1
    return n_plists, n_links




def bundles(root, plugins=True):
    for name in sorted(os.listdir(root)):
        if not name.endswith('.kext'):
            continue
        kext = os.path.join(root, name)
        info = os.path.join(kext, 'Contents', 'Info.plist')
        exe_dir = os.path.join(kext, 'Contents', 'MacOS')
        plug = os.path.join(kext, 'Contents', 'PlugIns')
        if not os.path.exists(info):                 # flat bundle layout
            info, exe_dir, plug = (os.path.join(kext, 'Info.plist'),
                                   kext, os.path.join(kext, 'PlugIns'))
        # A .kext with no Info.plist at all is not a bundle, but it may still
        # hold PlugIns that are: the KDK's iPodDriver.kext is nothing but a
        # Contents/PlugIns holding com.apple.driver.iPodSBCDriver, which is in
        # the manifest and in kmutil's collection.  Keep descending.
        if os.path.exists(info):
            try:
                pl = plistlib.load(open(info, 'rb'))
            except Exception:
                pl = None
            if pl is not None:
                yield pl.get('CFBundleIdentifier'), (
                    os.path.join(exe_dir, pl['CFBundleExecutable'])
                    if pl.get('CFBundleExecutable') else None)
        if plugins:
            seen = set()
            for p in (plug, os.path.join(kext, 'Contents', 'PlugIns'),
                      os.path.join(kext, 'PlugIns')):
                if p in seen or not os.path.isdir(p):
                    continue
                seen.add(p)
                yield from bundles(p, plugins=False)

# The slice names `lipo -archs` would print, read straight out of the Mach-O
# instead: this script has to run on the Linux build host too, where there is
# no lipo (base/darwin/toolchain/build-dyld-app-cache-util.sh).
_CPU = {
    (0x0100000C, 0): 'arm64',  (0x0100000C, 1): 'arm64v8', (0x0100000C, 2): 'arm64e',
    (0x0200000C, 1): 'arm64_32',
    (0x01000007, 3): 'x86_64', (0x01000007, 8): 'x86_64h',
    (0x00000007, 3): 'i386',
    (0x0000000C, 9): 'armv7',  (0x0000000C, 11): 'armv7s',
}

def _arch_name(cputype, cpusubtype):
    key = (cputype, cpusubtype & 0x00FFFFFF)
    return _CPU.get(key, '0x%x:%d' % key)

def macho_archs(path):
    """Slice architectures of a thin or fat Mach-O, as lipo -archs names them."""
    try:
        with open(path, 'rb') as f:
            head = f.read(4096)
    except OSError:
        return []
    if len(head) < 8:
        return []
    magic = struct.unpack('>I', head[:4])[0]
    if magic in (0xCAFEBABE, 0xCAFEBABF):            # fat, headers are big endian
        wide = (magic == 0xCAFEBABF)
        n    = struct.unpack('>I', head[4:8])[0]
        step = 32 if wide else 20
        out  = []
        for i in range(n):
            off = 8 + i * step
            if off + 8 > len(head):
                break
            ct, cs = struct.unpack('>iI', head[off:off + 8])
            out.append(_arch_name(ct & 0xFFFFFFFF, cs))
        return out
    if magic in (0xFEEDFACE, 0xFEEDFACF):            # thin, big endian
        ct, cs = struct.unpack('>iI', head[4:12])
    elif struct.unpack('<I', head[:4])[0] in (0xFEEDFACE, 0xFEEDFACF):
        ct, cs = struct.unpack('<iI', head[4:12])
    else:
        return []
    return [_arch_name(ct & 0xFFFFFFFF, cs)]



def filter_ids(ext_dir, ids):
    """(kept, dropped): the ids dyld_app_cache_util can load, and why each other one cannot."""
    archs = {}
    for bid, exe in bundles(ext_dir):
        if bid is None:
            continue
        if exe is None or not os.path.exists(exe):
            archs[bid] = 'codeless'
            continue
        out = macho_archs(exe)
        archs[bid] = 'arm64e' if 'arm64e' in out else ('bad:' + ','.join(out) if out else 'bad:none')

    kept, dropped = [], []
    for bid in ids:
        if bid.startswith('com.apple.kpi.'):
            dropped.append('drop %-45s symbol-set pseudo-kext' % bid); continue
        state = archs.get(bid)
        if state is None:
            dropped.append('drop %-45s not found in %s' % (bid, ext_dir)); continue
        if state.startswith('bad:'):
            dropped.append('drop %-45s no arm64e slice (%s)' % (bid, state[4:])); continue
        kept.append(bid)
    return kept, dropped


PRELINK_EXTRA = """<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
%s	<key>ManagerVersion</key>
	<integer>1</integer>
	<key>OSPrelinkInfoContainsUUIDs</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
"""


def die(msg):
    sys.exit('bench-kc-build: error: ' + msg)


def note(msg):
    print('bench-kc-build: ' + msg, flush=True)


def default_kdk():
    if os.environ.get('KDKROOT'):
        return os.environ['KDKROOT']
    kdks = sorted(glob.glob('/Library/Developer/KDKs/KDK_%s_*.kdk' % os.environ.get('MACOS_VERSION', '26.5')))
    if len(kdks) > 1:
        die('more than one KDK for MACOS_VERSION; pass --kdk one of: ' + ' '.join(kdks))
    return kdks[0] if kdks else ''


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog='bench-kc-build', description=__doc__,
                                 formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    ap.add_argument('--kernel', required=True)
    ap.add_argument('--kdk', default=None)
    ap.add_argument('--kc-type', required=True)
    ap.add_argument('--kernel-config', default='DEVELOPMENT')
    ap.add_argument('--arch', default='arm64e')
    ap.add_argument('--kmbuildversion', default='')
    ap.add_argument('--ref-kc', default='')
    ap.add_argument('--text-exec-order', default=os.environ.get('KCB_TEXT_EXEC_ORDER', 'kexts-first'),
                    choices=('kexts-first', 'kernel-first'))
    ap.add_argument('--out', required=True)
    ap.add_argument('--task', default='kc')
    ap.add_argument('--variant', default='')
    ap.add_argument('--soc', default='unknown')
    args = ap.parse_args()

    if args.kdk is None:
        args.kdk = default_kdk()
    if not os.path.isfile(args.kernel):
        die('no kernel at ' + args.kernel)
    if not os.path.isdir(args.kdk):
        die('no KDK at ' + args.kdk)
    # It hardcodes arm64e/macOS, which is every collection this bench builds;
    # fail loudly rather than silently ignoring a request for something else.
    if args.arch != 'arm64e':
        die('--arch %s: only arm64e is supported' % args.arch)
    tool = os.environ.get('KCB_TOOL') or shutil.which('dyld_app_cache_util')
    if not tool or not os.access(tool, os.X_OK):
        die('no dyld_app_cache_util on PATH; build it with base/darwin/toolchain/build-dyld-app-cache-util.sh')

    # Byte identity needs the KDK at its real macOS path; warn rather than
    # fail, because a merely-correct collection is still useful.
    if not re.match(r'^/Library/Developer/KDKs/.*\.kdk/?$', args.kdk):
        print('bench-kc-build: warning: KDK is at %s, not /Library/Developer/KDKs/...' % args.kdk, file=sys.stderr)
        print("bench-kc-build: warning: the collection will be correct but not byte-identical to kmutil's", file=sys.stderr)

    kdk = args.kdk.rstrip('/')
    kc_variant = args.kernel_config.lower()
    extensions = os.path.join(kdk, 'System/Library/Extensions')
    manifest = os.path.join(kdk, 'System/Library/KernelCollections',
                            'kernelcache.release.%s.manifest.plist' % args.kc_type)
    if not os.path.isfile(manifest):
        die('no manifest ' + manifest)

    # KMBuildVersion is the project version of the kmutil whose output we are
    # matching. There is no kmutil on Linux: it comes from --kmbuildversion, or
    # from a collection built on a Mac, whose __PRELINK_INFO carries it verbatim.
    km_build_version = args.kmbuildversion
    if not km_build_version and args.ref_kc:
        with open(args.ref_kc, 'rb') as f:
            m = re.search(rb'<key>KMBuildVersion</key>[ \t\r\n]*<string>([^<]*)</string>', f.read())
        km_build_version = m.group(1).decode() if m else ''
        if km_build_version:
            note('kmver read from ' + args.ref_kc)
    if not km_build_version:
        # Neither xnu nor dyld reads it; only kmutil's bytes need it.
        note('no --kmbuildversion / --ref-kc: KMBuildVersion left out, so not byte-identical to kmutil')

    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:
        # 1. A staging mirror of the KDK's Extensions with kmutil's Info.plists.
        #    -volume-root makes _PrelinkBundlePath come back out as the real
        #    /Library/Developer/KDKs/... path.
        stage_root = os.path.join(tmp, 'stage')
        src = os.path.realpath(extensions)
        staged = os.path.join(stage_root, src.lstrip('/'))
        os.makedirs(staged, exist_ok=True)
        n_plists, n_links = stage(src, staged, src, args.arch, kc_variant or None)
        note('stage    %d Info.plists rewritten, %d files linked' % (n_plists, n_links))

        # 2. The manifest's requiredIdentifiers minus $KC_FILTER, then minus
        #    what this builder cannot take.
        with open(manifest, 'rb') as f:
            ids = plistlib.load(f)['requiredIdentifiers']
        drop_re = os.environ.get('KC_FILTER', '')
        if drop_re:
            ids = [b for b in ids if not re.search(drop_re, b)]
        kept, dropped = filter_ids(staged, ids)
        kpi = [b for b in ids if re.match(r'com\.apple\.kpi\.', b)]

        # 3. The three top-level keys KernelManagement stamps on the plist.
        extra = os.path.join(tmp, 'prelink-extra.plist')
        with open(extra, 'w') as f:
            f.write(PRELINK_EXTRA % ('\t<key>KMBuildVersion</key>\n\t<string>%s</string>\n' % km_build_version
                                     if km_build_version else ''))

        note('task     %s%s' % (args.task, ' (%s)' % args.variant if args.variant else ''))
        note('kdk      ' + kdk)
        note('kernel   ' + args.kernel)
        note('kmver    ' + (km_build_version or '(none)'))
        note('filter   ' + (drop_re or '(none)'))
        # patches/0004-text-exec-order-env.patch: kexts-first (dyld-1378 default) or
        # kernel-first (pre-1378 order, required by xnu <= 12377.81 / macOS 26.3).
        note('textexec ' + args.text_exec_order)
        note('kexts    %d requested, %d linked, %d codeless symbol sets' % (len(ids), len(kept), len(kpi)))
        for line in dropped:
            print('bench-kc-build:   ' + line, file=sys.stderr)

        kc = os.path.join(tmp, 'kc')
        cmd = [tool, '-create-kernel-collection', kc,
               '-arch', 'arm64e', '-platform', 'macOS',
               '-kernel', args.kernel,
               '-extensions', staged,
               '-volume-root', stage_root,
               '-kext-variant', kc_variant,
               '-prelink-info-extra', extra]
        for b in kept:
            cmd += ['-bundle-id', b]
        for b in kpi:
            cmd += ['-codeless-bundle-id', b]
        env = dict(os.environ, KCB_TEXT_EXEC_ORDER=args.text_exec_order)
        rc = subprocess.run(cmd, env=env).returncode
        if rc != 0:
            die('dyld_app_cache_util exited %d (a kernel compiled from source needs KC_FILTER=com.apple.driver.SEPHibernation)' % rc)
        if not os.path.isfile(kc):
            die('the builder produced nothing')
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.out)), exist_ok=True)
        shutil.move(kc, args.out)

    with open(args.out, 'rb') as f:
        digest = hashlib.sha256(f.read()).hexdigest()
    note('wrote %s (%d bytes, sha256 %s)' % (args.out, os.path.getsize(args.out), digest))


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
